  "section_notes": "The final package keeps the 5% thermal test limit and 8/100k recall trigger, satisfying Halcyon's core safety asks, while giving Northwind its red lines: per-model test results go to customers and regulators but are not publicly published, retrofit deadline is 6 years, and suppression starts at 36 months. S1 requires all incidents reported within 5 days, which is later than the safe 48-hour serious-incident deadline. S2 lacks a retest requirement for existing models, and S3's 2-year new-unit deadline is weaker than the acceptable 12 months."
